Oracle
------
A black barrier at alpha a composites source-over in 8-bit sRGB as
    dimmed = original * (1 - a)
so per channel  a = 1 - dimmed/original.
Two full-frame screencaps of the SAME screen (sheet closed / sheet open) are
differenced over a region the barrier covers but the sheet does not.
Sampling region: x 0..1344, y 160..560 (device px) — below the status bar,
above the sheet's top edge (~y 600). Channel samples with original < 60 are
discarded (no signal). 537,600 pixels -> 1,114,285 usable channel samples.

Region validity (row scout, 80px bands, guard build):
  y 160..560  median a = 0.2000-0.2031, 100.0% of samples within +/-0.02
  y 560..640  consistency collapses to 66-73% -> sheet edge
  y >= 640    incoherent (sheet content, not barrier)
0.0% of pixels in the sampled region are byte-identical between the two frames,
i.e. the barrier demonstrably composited over every sampled pixel.

